## 0. How to use this doc

You are about to claim one feature and ship it end-to-end. Before you touch any code:

1. Read `CLAUDE.md` (root) — the 12-section operating rules. Not optional.
2. Read the feature card in §8 of this doc for the feature you are claiming.
3. Read the four upstream docs that card references (they are always the same four: `03-architecture.md`, `06-contracts.md`, `02-ideas.md`, and the prompt block in `05-merged-plan.md` if your feature owns a prompt).
4. Write your **feature plan addendum** (§9.2 template) into a scratch note or into this file under §11 Decision log. Get alignment before you code.
5. Implement against the ports and events already defined. **Do not invent new ports or events without a §7 RFC.**
6. Run the tripwires in §10. All green = you are done. Any red = not done.

The first agent to claim a feature wins the folder. Two agents must never be inside the same `features/<name>/` at the same time. Coordination is by folder ownership, not by lock files.

