## 2. Production end-state — what "done" looks like

A citizen — call her Maria — opens `clara.app` on any device. In under 30 seconds she answers three questions. In under 5 seconds after that, a dark, voice-first dashboard shows her three policy cards she actually needs to know about, each one cited back to a line of the law it came from. She taps one. A warm voice in her language speaks the briefing to her while the citations highlight in sync. A media panel shows her what the press said about this policy versus what it actually does. A watchlist queues three ongoing topics she should monitor next month, with exact deadlines and the physical office she'd walk into. She never created an account, never uploaded a document, never saw a "GPT-4 powered" tag, never saw a single error toast.

Under the hood, at production grade:

- **10 sealed feature modules** (F1–F9 required, F11 behind a flag), each one end-to-end testable in isolation via its own contract tests + one integration test against the real event bus.
- **Real ingestion**: a Python scraper running on a schedule in Hugging Face Spaces (or as a one-shot cron job) hitting `bundesregierung.de`, `bmas.de`, `bamf.de`, `muenchen.de`, `gesetze-im-internet.de`. On failure, the system falls back to `seed/policies.json` — no user-visible degradation.
- **Real Claude + ElevenLabs** behind the `LLMPort` and `VoicePort`, with the `VoiceCircuitBreaker` wired and proven (kill switch test in CI).
- **Real Postgres + pgvector** via Neon serverless, reachable from HF Spaces over TLS. A SQLite fallback adapter exists for local dev but is never used in prod.
- **Real citations**: every sentence of every briefing is either cite-locked (`[[span_N]]` → resolvable `PolicySpan`) or the briefing is rejected and regenerated. This is the trust layer; it is non-negotiable.
- **Five personas** (Maria, Hakan, Greta, Leila, Sofia) live as seed data, selectable via a dev-only `?persona=` query param so judges can re-roll live.
- **Deployed**: `clara.app` (Vercel static SPA) talks to `api.clara.app` (HF Spaces FastAPI over HTTPS) which talks to Neon Postgres + Claude + ElevenLabs. One-click redeploys on push to `main`.
- **Observable**: structured JSON logs (stdout → HF Spaces log tail) with `feature`, `persona_id`, `trace_id`, `event`. Sentry DSN wired for client errors. No OTel/Jaeger — cut per `05-merged-plan.md §5`.
- **Every tripwire green**: `ruff`, `import-linter`, `mypy --strict`, `eslint` (including FSD boundaries), `tsc --noEmit`, contract tests, the one Maria E2E test, the one Greta E2E test.

If all of that is true, the product is production-grade by hackathon standards. Everything beyond (Berlin feeds, WASM embedding, Rust scraper, OTel, push notifications) is `02-ideas.md` F12 post-hack territory — not in scope for this roadmap.

