## 4. Data model (production grade)

All types are Pydantic `BaseModel`s in `packages/contracts/schemas/`. This is the canonical list — `06-contracts.md §3` is the source of truth, this section is an operational index.

### 4.1 Entity map

```mermaid
erDiagram
  PERSONA ||--o{ BRIEFING : "generated for"
  PERSONA ||--o{ WATCH_ITEM : "owns"
  POLICY  ||--o{ POLICY_CHUNK : "chunked into"
  POLICY_CHUNK ||--o{ POLICY_SPAN : "anchors"
  POLICY  ||--o{ BRIEFING : "source for"
  BRIEFING ||--o{ CITATION : "contains"
  CITATION }o--|| POLICY_SPAN : "resolves to"
  POLICY  ||--o| MEDIA_ANALYSIS : "analyzed as"
```

### 4.2 Postgres schema (target, prod)

Managed by `apps/api/migrations/NNN_*.sql`. Each migration is a single logical change, numbered, forward-only.

```sql
-- 001_init.sql
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;

CREATE TABLE personas (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  profile       JSONB NOT NULL,               -- PersonaProfile serialized
  embedding     VECTOR(1024),                 -- for feed cosine search
  created_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
CREATE INDEX personas_embedding_idx
  ON personas USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops);

CREATE TABLE policies (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  title         TEXT NOT NULL,
  source_name   TEXT NOT NULL,
  source_url    TEXT NOT NULL,
  raw_text      TEXT NOT NULL,
  tags          TEXT[] NOT NULL,
  affected_groups TEXT[] NOT NULL,
  urgency       TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (urgency IN ('low','medium','high')),
  scraped_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
  inserted_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE policy_chunks (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  policy_id     TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES policies(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  ordinal       INT  NOT NULL,
  text          TEXT NOT NULL,
  embedding     VECTOR(1024) NOT NULL,
  UNIQUE (policy_id, ordinal)
);
CREATE INDEX policy_chunks_embedding_idx
  ON policy_chunks USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops);
CREATE INDEX policy_chunks_policy_idx ON policy_chunks(policy_id);

CREATE TABLE policy_spans (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,             -- "span_42"
  policy_id     TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES policies(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  chunk_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES policy_chunks(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  section       TEXT NOT NULL,                -- "§12 Abs. 3"
  text          TEXT NOT NULL,
  char_start    INT  NOT NULL,
  char_end      INT  NOT NULL
);
CREATE INDEX policy_spans_policy_idx ON policy_spans(policy_id);

CREATE TABLE briefings (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  persona_id    TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES personas(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  policy_id     TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES policies(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  payload       JSONB NOT NULL,               -- full Briefing serialized
  language      TEXT NOT NULL,
  generated_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
  UNIQUE (persona_id, policy_id)
);
CREATE INDEX briefings_persona_idx ON briefings(persona_id);

CREATE TABLE media_analyses (
  policy_id     TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES policies(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  payload       JSONB NOT NULL,
  generated_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE watch_items (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  persona_id    TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES personas(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  payload       JSONB NOT NULL,
  created_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
CREATE INDEX watch_items_persona_idx ON watch_items(persona_id);
```

**Rules of this schema**:

- `id` is always `TEXT`, human-inspectable (`"persona_maria_01"`, `"policy_bund_2026_0017"`). No surrogate `SERIAL` ids — they obscure event payloads during debugging.
- Every vector is 1024-dim (Claude embedding dimension) and indexed with HNSW cosine ops.
- `payload JSONB` holds the full Pydantic-serialized entity; individual columns exist only for what we filter or index on. This keeps schema migrations cheap when a domain model grows a field.
- Every table has a cascading FK back to its owning persona or policy — deleting a persona cleans up their entire derived state. This matters for the "your profile never leaves your browser" pitch: we must be able to prove there's a delete path.

### 4.3 Repository binding (contract: `core/ports/repository.py`)

At composition root, one `Repository[T]` is instantiated per entity:

```python
Container(
    personas   = vector.repository("personas"),
    policies   = vector.repository("policies"),
    briefings  = vector.repository("briefings"),
    watchitems = vector.repository("watch_items"),
    # media_analyses is owned by media_analysis feature, bound as Repository[MediaAnalysis]
)
```

The day-1 scaffold uses `InMemoryRepository[T]` for every one of these. The Neon/pgvector adapter replaces them at prod wire-time via the composition root — **zero feature code changes**. That swap is exactly the "how did you get to production in a day" answer.

