## 10. Tripwires — the automated gates

These are the checks that turn architectural intent into compile errors. They must all be green on `main` at all times. An agent's PR does not merge if any one of them is red.

### 10.1 Static tripwires (pre-merge, in CI and pre-commit)

| Tripwire | Command | Catches |
|---|---|---|
| Python lint | `cd apps/api && uv run ruff check src` | Style, imports, unused vars, some common bugs. |
| Python types | `cd apps/api && uv run mypy src` | All type errors in strict mode. `Any` is forbidden without justification. |
| Python boundaries | `cd apps/api && uv run lint-imports` | Feature-to-feature imports, feature-to-infra imports, core-to-outward imports. |
| TS lint | `cd apps/web && bunx eslint .` | Style, boundaries (FSD layer order), unused vars. |
| TS types | `cd apps/web && bunx tsc -b --noEmit` | All type errors. `strictNullChecks`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`. |
| TS-from-Pydantic codegen | `bash packages/contracts/gen-types.sh && git diff --exit-code packages/contracts/generated/` | Stale or hand-edited generated types. |

### 10.2 Runtime tripwires (pre-merge, CI)

| Tripwire | What it asserts |
|---|---|
| `/health` smoke test | FastAPI app boots; every feature's `wire()` runs without raising; the subscription graph is logged with every expected event name present. |
| Handler integration tests | For each feature with a subscriber, emit the upstream event against a real `AsyncioEventBus` and assert the downstream event fires with the right payload. |
| Contract tests per port | One test suite per port; every adapter (real + mock) must pass the same suite. This is what lets a vendor swap happen in CI, not in code review. |
| E2E Maria | Scripted: onboard → feed → translate → voice → citations. Asserts ≥3 feed cards, ≥1 citation resolved, audio stream returns bytes. Runs against mock adapters so it's deterministic in CI. |
| E2E Greta | Same flow, different persona. This is the "universality re-roll" proof. |
| Circuit-breaker drill | Force `ElevenLabsAdapter.stream()` to raise twice in a row; assert the third call returns `LocalMp3Adapter` bytes. Part of F6's DoD. |

### 10.3 Demo-day tripwires (manual checklist, day-of)

The `05-merged-plan.md §9` pre-demo checklist is the source of truth for the day-of rituals. This roadmap does not duplicate it — it defers to that doc.

### 10.4 What happens when a tripwire goes red

1. **Static red** → the PR cannot merge. Fix the code or update the contract with an RFC. Never disable a tripwire to unblock a PR.
2. **Runtime red** → same, plus: read the failing test, don't just re-run CI. Flaky tests are bugs, not noise.
3. **Codegen red** (`git diff --exit-code` failed) → someone edited the generated TS by hand, or someone edited a schema and forgot to regenerate. Run `bash packages/contracts/gen-types.sh` and commit the diff.
4. **A tripwire that has never failed before suddenly fails** → treat it as a real bug, not a test-infra hiccup. The tripwires are designed to only fail on real boundary violations.

