### 12.2 Wave order — who can start when

**Wave 0 · already shipped** (the scaffold, on `main`):
- Monorepo shape, composition root, 9 sealed feature stubs, ports + adapters, InMemory repos, AsyncioEventBus, `/health`, FE FSD skeleton, all tripwires green.

**Wave 1 · no blockers, start immediately in parallel** (5 agents can claim now):
- **agent-A** → F1 Onboarding, then F2 Persona Builder (same branch lineage, two commits).
- **agent-E** → F9 Ingestion + seed file. Must land **before** agent-B's F3 can produce real output (F3 can start against seed fixtures in parallel, but it can't demo without real policies).
- **agent-B** → F3 Feed (can scaffold against fixtures until F9 lands; real end-to-end requires F9 + F2).
- **agent-C** → F4 Translator, then F5 Citations. Can scaffold immediately but requires F9 spans for real cite-locking.
- **agent-D** → F6 Voice (vendor side — the feature folder is unblocked immediately because `briefing.generated` can be mocked in the handler test; real integration requires F4).

**Wave 2 · requires Wave 1 partial** (these start when their upstream publishes working events):
- F7 Media Analysis (agent-D, after F3 can emit `card.selected` — which the FE does directly, so after F3's dashboard ships).
- F8 Watchlist (agent-B, after F2 ships `persona.persisted`).

**Wave 3 · stretch, only if Wave 1 + 2 are green by H9**:
- F11 Consequence Tree. Requires a new event in the catalog (RFC-first).

**Parallel-safe cross-cutting work** (any idle agent picks this up):
- **Audio baking**: pre-bake 5 fallback MP3s into `apps/api/public/audio/` per persona, using one call to ElevenLabs per persona. This is an **ops task**, not a feature — it touches no feature code. It's the first thing an idle agent should do because F6 depends on the files existing.
- **Neon DB provisioning + migration apply**: a one-time ops task to create the prod Neon branch and run `apps/api/migrations/001_init.sql`. Blocks the prod deploy but not local development.
- **HF Spaces image build**: write `apps/api/Dockerfile` (uv-based FastAPI image) and configure the HF Space. Blocks the prod deploy.
- **Vercel project setup**: link `apps/web` to a Vercel project, configure `VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.clara.app`. Blocks the prod deploy.

### 12.3 Critical path (the one line that cannot slip)

The critical path for a demo-ready product is:

```
F9 (seed data) → F2 (persona) → F3 (feed) → F4 (translator) → F6 (voice) → E2E Maria
```

If any single one of these slips, the demo cannot run. Everything else (F7 Media Panel, F8 Watchlist, F11 Consequence Tree) is cuttable without losing the demo.

**Agent claim priorities for a fresh pool** of agents (in order):
1. **agent-E F9** (unblocks three downstreams)
2. **agent-A F1→F2** (unblocks two downstreams)
3. **agent-C F4** (critical path; F5 follows naturally under same agent)
4. **agent-B F3** (can start against fixtures, finalize once F9 lands)
5. **agent-D F6** (critical path; F7 follows under same agent)
6. Everything else is parallel.

### 12.4 Go/no-go gates for promotion to prod

The roadmap has three gates. Ship only what passes the gate.

**Gate G1 · local green**: all tripwires (§10) green on the developer's machine.
**Gate G2 · CI green**: same tripwires green in CI, including E2E Maria and Greta flows.
**Gate G3 · prod smoke**: after deploy, `/health` returns 200 on `api.clara.app`, and the live Vercel URL renders the dashboard end-to-end as Maria.

No feature is "done" until it passes all three gates. Gate G3 is the difference between "works on my machine" and "judges will see it".

### 12.5 Demo-day freeze

On the day of the demo, `main` is frozen at 08:00 local. No merges after the freeze — only hotfix cherry-picks to a `demo/<date>` branch, signed off by two agents. This is the pre-demo ritual equivalent to a release train.

