## 13. Closing directive — to any agent reading this

You are one of several. You have been given one folder, one card, and one contract. Everything you need to ship your feature end-to-end is either in your `features/<name>/` folder or behind a port that already exists. If you find yourself reaching outside that folder, you are either doing the wrong thing or discovering an RFC — stop and figure out which.

The architecture is not ceremony. It is the coordination mechanism that lets five of you ship a production-grade civic briefing system in one day without ever reading each other's code. Respect it, and the system respects you back with zero merge conflicts. Violate it, and a tripwire will tell you so before the user ever sees your mistake.

Read your card. Write your plan. Ship your feature. Update the log.

**Pitch the human. Defend with the architecture.**
